# Normalize text in-repo to LF (the blobs already are); platform checkouts vary
# by the rules below. Last matching rule wins per attribute.
* text=auto eol=crlf

# Hashed asset bytes must be identical on every checkout, every OS, every CI
# runner: no end-of-line conversion, ever. CI run #1 caught exactly this —
# converted SVG line endings broke the pack's SHA-256 integrity checks.
assets/** -text
*.svg -text
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.pdf binary
*.ocfproj binary

# Shell scripts and git hooks MUST check out with LF on every platform. The
# repository-wide eol=crlf above would otherwise hand a Linux or macOS clone a
# `#!/bin/sh` line ending in , which fails as "bad interpreter" — silently
# disabling the pre-commit secret scan for precisely the contributors who did
# not write it. Protection that does not run still reads as protection.
.githooks/** text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
